{
  "name": "ANet brand palette",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "date": "2026-10-03",
  "notes": [
    "Primitive scales designed in OKLCH; red.500 is pinned to the logo red #E93024.",
    "gray = \"Graphite\" cool-neutral tech gray (OKLCH hue 255, chroma <= 0.011).",
    "Red is for emphasis and key states only: one key action, failure, warning signal, focus, brand marks.",
    "Success and info stay in the neutral system (ink + check icon); warning = red signal on calm text; danger = solid red.",
    "Never rely on colour alone: every status carries its icon (circle-check / triangle-alert / circle-x / info).",
    "Contrast: text pairs >= 4.5:1, UI and graphic pairs >= 3:1 (WCAG 2.2 AA, 1.4.3 / 1.4.11). See \"contrast\".",
    "accent.brand (#E93024) is 4.27:1 on white: use it for marks, rules, icons, focus rings and large display type, not for body text or button labels on light backgrounds; use accent.fg / accent.solid there."
  ],
